description:
Pursuant to the Oklahoma Open Records Act (51 O.S. Section 24A.1 et seq.), the Move Weight Foundation requests access to and copies of the following City of Miami records concerning the City Attorney position, the July 28, 2026 citywide email referenced publicly by former City Attorney Misty Barnes, and city-held records related to public allegations about the handling of photographs or confidential information connected to the April 17, 2025 fatal crash that killed Nicholas and Sharon Malpass.

For all items below, please search records from January 1, 2025 through the date this request is fulfilled unless a narrower date is specified.

1. Misty Barnes's resignation letter, notice of resignation, acceptance, effective date, final work day, final pay or compensation records, contract amendments, separation agreement, severance records, transition memos, exit interview notes, and any records explaining or discussing the reason for separation from the City Attorney position.

2. The citywide email Ms. Barnes publicly stated she sent on July 28, 2026 after leaving the City Attorney position, including the original message, subject line, attachments, recipient list, distribution list, delivery metadata, forwarding records, reply chains, any recall or edit attempts, and any related communications about that email.

3. All emails, text messages, memoranda, meeting notes, calendar entries, attachments, and other communications between or among Misty Barnes, Mayor Bless Parker, City Manager Tyler Cline, City Clerk Melissa Moore, Communications Manager Melinda Stotts, City Council members, Miami Police Department leadership, and any outside counsel concerning any of the following topics:
   a. the April 17, 2025 fatal crash involving Nicholas and Sharon Malpass;
   b. public allegations that a young person's photograph or confidential information was shared, described, verified, or used by a city official or city employee;
   c. statements or complaints by the Stotts family, Cori Stotts, or any family member referenced in public posts or city council comments;
   d. any effort to verify family connections, identify persons in photographs, or discuss the propriety of sharing photographs or juvenile-related information;
   e. public comments, social media posts, press inquiries, or communications strategy concerning these allegations;
   f. Ottawa County District Court matter CJ-2026-0110, to the extent records are held by the City and are not lawfully exempt.

4. All City policies, procedures, training materials, retention rules, legal opinions, or directives concerning the handling, sharing, preservation, redaction, or public discussion of photographs, juvenile information, confidential records, accident records, and records involving minors or young persons.

5. All complaints, grievances, internal reviews, investigative records, disciplinary records, council agenda items, public-session records, and non-exempt executive-session minutes or action records concerning Misty Barnes, the City Attorney office, or any City employee's handling of the photograph/confidential-information allegations described above.

6. All communications with the Ottawa County District Attorney, Ottawa County officials, outside counsel, insurers, or law enforcement agencies concerning the same topics.

If any record is withheld, please provide a privilege/exemption log identifying the date, sender, recipient, general subject matter, and the specific Oklahoma statute or legal basis claimed for withholding. Please release all reasonably segregable non-exempt portions of responsive records. Please provide an itemized fee estimate before incurring fees, and provide records electronically where available.
